  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `IncomingCommunicationJobHandler.cs` (email inbound job — the lock/check/persist/mark + DLQ ordering to mirror), `IIdempotencyService`/`IdempotencyService`/`DeadLetterQueueService`, `GraphMessageNormalizer.cs` (the normalizer shape), `NormalizedMessage.cs`, and task 021's `ICommunicationChannelIngestor`/`MessagingIngestor`. Read the job-envelope contract 030 enqueues.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `.claude/agent-memory/researcher/acs-chat-integration-2026-07-16.md` + design §4/§8.3 for exact ACS event fields (message id, thread id, sender `communicationUserId`, content, timestamp) and the at-least-once/duplicate/echo semantics. Grep-confirm no ACS normalizer + no messaging job handler exist (§11 evidence).</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the ACS-event normalizer: map the ACS `ChatMessageReceivedInThread` (+ siblings) payload → `NormalizedMessage` (Direction=Incoming; From = sender; BodyText/BodyHtml; SentAt; ACS `ChatThreadId` → `ConversationId`; attachments as `NormalizedAttachment` descriptors). Map exactly once at the boundary; no `Azure.Communication.*` leaks past it.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the Service Bus job handler (`IJobHandler` for the new job kind from 030): (a) `TryAcquireProcessingLockAsync(acsMessageId)` — if not acquired (concurrent duplicate in flight), no-op; (b) `IsEventProcessedAsync(acsMessageId)` — if already processed (redelivery / prior duplicate / our own outbound echo), no-op; (c) normalize + call `MessagingIngestor.IngestAsync(normalizedMessage)` to persist + enrich best-effort; (d) `MarkEventAsProcessedAsync(acsMessageId)`; (e) release the lock. Order (persist before mark) so a crash between persist and mark re-processes but the mark/lock still prevents a second persist — verify the ingestor persist itself tolerates this (or the mark covers it). Ensure the invariant: exactly one `sprk_communication` per ACS message id.</step>
    <step order="5">Wire DLQ: on repeated failure past the contract's retry/backoff, dead-letter the job to Storage via `DeadLetterQueueService`; never silently drop. Keep enrichment/thread side-effects best-effort (NFR-02) — a persist succeeds even if enrichment throws.</step>
    <step order="6">Register the normalizer + handler in `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010; ADR-032 Null-Object + unconditional if feature-gated).</step>
    <step order="7">Write tests (integration-heavy, ADR-038 vertical-slice seam — no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`): (a) single inbound event → one `sprk_communication`; (b) SAME event delivered twice → still exactly one record (dedupe); (c) our own outbound message id already marked → the echo event is a no-op (zero new records); (d) two concurrent deliveries of the same id → exactly one persist (lock race); (e) repeated processing failure → job dead-lettered to Storage, not dropped; (f) enrichment throws → the `sprk_communication` is still persisted (NFR-02).</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`; confirm existing inbound/job tests still pass.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/msg-031-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline. ≥+5 MB justify; ≥55 MB architecture review; ≥60 MB HARD STOP.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (EXPLICIT focus on the idempotency/echo-dedup correctness + lock ordering + DLQ-not-drop); `adr-check` against `spec.md` (NFR-02/03, FR-02/04, ADR-004/036 reuse, ADR-045 boundary-normalize-once). Resolve Critical findings (path C) or surface an ADR conflict (root §6.5).</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` + `Services/Jobs/` BFF hot-path).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (031 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (dedupe key = ACS message id; lock/check/persist/mark ordering; DLQ trigger; the `sprk_thread` field is deliberately left for 040).</step>
  </steps>

