  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">An ACS `ChatMessageReceivedInThread` event is normalized to a `NormalizedMessage` (Direction=Incoming; ACS `ChatThreadId` → `ConversationId`) exactly once at the boundary; no `Azure.Communication.*` type appears downstream of the normalizer.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A single inbound event persists exactly one `sprk_communication` (type=Message) via `MessagingIngestor`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Duplicate delivery of the same ACS message id yields exactly one persisted record (dedupe via `IIdempotencyService` on the ACS message id — NFR-03).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Event Grid echo of our own outbound message is a no-op — the already-recorded outbound ACS message id causes zero additional persists (FR-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Two concurrent deliveries of the same id result in exactly one persist (processing-lock race resolved cleanly).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Repeated processing failure dead-letters the job to Storage via `DeadLetterQueueService` — the message is never silently dropped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An enrichment/thread-assignment failure does NOT fail the persist — the `sprk_communication` is still written (NFR-02).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The `sprk_thread` lookup is NOT set by this task (left to 040); no outbound send path is built here (051); no client-side ACS SDK is introduced.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; existing inbound/job tests pass; publish-size delta reported vs ~45.30 MB (≤60 MB); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on 030 (the Event Grid ingress + the job envelope this handler consumes) and 021 (the `ICommunicationChannelIngestor` seam + `MessagingIngestor` this handler calls). Blocks 040 (`IThreadResolver` sets `sprk_thread` on the record this task persists) and 051 (outbound persist-on-send relies on THIS task's echo-dedup to keep the echo a no-op). `parallel-safe: false` — serial after 030 (consumes 030's job contract; correctness-critical idempotency must not race with the ingress change). `sonnet @ xhigh` — the idempotency + echo-dedup + lock-ordering correctness under at-least-once delivery is the crux of the inbound spine.

    Strict scope: normalizer + idempotent handler + DLQ. Thread assignment (040), outbound send (051), and the Event Grid ingress (030) are separate. Reuse `IIdempotencyService` + `DeadLetterQueueService` verbatim — do NOT hand-roll dedupe or a second DLQ. The invariant to defend in review: exactly one persisted `sprk_communication` per distinct ACS message id, across at-least-once redelivery, genuine duplicates, and our own outbound echo.
  </notes>

